	"subtitle": "The white walls of Ptah",
	"history": "We set out from Memphis, where Upper and Lower Egypt meet. Tradition holds that King Menes founded the city around 3100 BCE and for much of the Old Kingdom the kings ruled from here; its patron was Ptah, protector of craftsmen. A fitting God, we thought, to see off a party of travellers with a chest full of amulets!",
